From 463cd3214073fc9b017b79f0625955ba0eda02d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Heider <andreas@heider.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:39:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] ipu7: asynchronous PSYS processing and zero-copy output

Drive the two PSYS stages from an EventNotifier on the PSYS fd instead
of blocking the pipeline thread, with a watchdog timer for stuck
firmware tasks. Only the newest waiting raw frame is processed.

Export NV12 buffers with a padded UV plane so the ISP writes its output
straight into application buffers; buffers that do not fit fall back to
copying from an internal output buffer. The IPA now receives a luma
histogram for tone adaptation instead of reading the output buffer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
